  "minimal_contract": [
    "Use one owned recovery cache created inside worker/private inlet; publish self._cache only after successful await and uncancelled/unexpired current owner admission.",
    "Propagate workflow absolute deadline through trace/ref iteration and load_entry into existing _read_entry(deadline_monotonic), and check deadline immediately before in-memory index admission.",
    "Simple two call off-loop mutation proves responsiveness, but actual timeout/cancellation returns leave worker capable of late seed into already exposed cache: forbid that ownership escape.",
    "FileSystemCAS is reusable across threads in existing get/put off-loop path and carries real filesystem readback; ContextVar tenant/access propagation must remain via existing context copy.",
    "run_blocking_async(None) imports30s default. Preserve intended no-workflow-deadline semantics explicitly; do not treat helper default as configured workflow deadline."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Physical synchronous read cannot be interrupted by asyncio cancellation; bounded observation measures admission and ready-loop responsiveness, not disk speed.",
    "Filesystem chmod denial and foreign bound scope were actual negatives; live/current institutional authorizer policy is not established.",
    "Naive control is a separate in-memory mutation, not a production candidate or green fix.",
    "First harness incorrectly applied success state assertion to expected deadline-fail result; preserved output-first-harness.txt is excluded from deciding evidence. Final rerun removes only that assertion for non-success cases.",
    "No full four-base replay or production dataset acceptance claim.",
    "Post-attempt real NodeResultCache.get and native _merge_cached_outcome_state read back late seeded entries and exact state operations; observation invokes the real consumer but does not claim the cancelled workflow resumed or committed that state.",
    "Final output-checkpoint.txt includes actual persisted CASCheckpointHook publication and latest-checkpoint resolution; prior output-consumer.txt is superseded by this complete source-identical runtime rerun."
  ],
